  "result": "Excellent! Both agents have completed their work, and all **371 tests pass** with the bulk discount feature fully implemented and tested! \n\n## Implementation Complete \u2705\n\n### **What Was Built**\n\n**Bulk Discount Feature:**\n- Lines with qty \u2265 10 automatically receive an additional **2.5% discount**\n- Applied to the remaining amount **after** line/tier discounts\n- VAT calculated on the final discounted amount\n- Included in `invoiceTotals` discount total\n\n### **Code Changes**\n\n1. **`src/totals.js`** - Added `lineBulkDiscount()` function and updated:\n   - `lineVAT()` to account for bulk discount\n   - `invoiceTotals()` to sum bulk discounts\n\n2. **`src/invoices.js`** - Re-exported `lineBulkDiscount` for backward compatibility\n\n3. **`test/totals.test.js`** - Added 35 comprehensive tests\n\n4. **`test/invoices.test.js`** & **`test/render.test.js`** - Updated 16 existing tests to match new calculations\n\n### **Example Calculation**\n\nFor a line with qty: 10, unitPrice: \u20ac95, with 5% tier discount:\n- Line total: \u20ac950.00\n- Line discount (5%): -\u20ac47.50\n- **Bulk discount (2.5% of \u20ac902.50): -\u20ac22.56**\n- Taxable amount: \u20ac880.00\n- VAT (21%): \u20ac184.80\n- **Final total: \u20ac1,064.80** (vs \u20ac1,092.02 without bulk discount)\n\n**Final Test Status:** 371 passing \u2705 | 0 failing | 0 skipped",
